@startuml AI Test Optimizer - Complete Workflow

title AI Test Optimizer - Complete Execution Flow

actor Developer
participant "GitHub Actions" as GH
participant "Test Optimizer CLI" as CLI
participant "TestAnalyzer" as Analyzer
participant "MLPredictor" as ML
participant "StrategyEngine" as Strategy
participant "ExecutionPlanner" as Planner
participant "TestExecutor" as Executor
participant "ReportGenerator" as Reporter
database "execution-history.json" as DB

== Initialization ==

Developer -> GH: Push code / Create PR
activate GH
GH -> CLI: npx ts-node src/test-optimizer/index.ts optimize balanced
activate CLI

CLI -> Analyzer: analyzeCodeChanges(changedFiles)
activate Analyzer
Analyzer -> Analyzer: parseGitDiff()
Analyzer -> Analyzer: extractChangedFiles()
Analyzer -> Analyzer: calculateComplexity()
Analyzer -> CLI: CodeChange[]
deactivate Analyzer

== Test Discovery ==

CLI -> Analyzer: discoverTests()
activate Analyzer
Analyzer -> Analyzer: scanFeatureFiles()
Analyzer -> Analyzer: parseGherkinScenarios()
Analyzer -> Analyzer: extractTestMetadata()
Analyzer -> CLI: TestCase[]
deactivate Analyzer

== ML Prediction ==

CLI -> ML: predictTestFailures(testCases, codeChanges)
activate ML

loop For each test case
    ML -> ML: extractFeatures(testCase)\n- historicalFailureRate\n- executionTime\n- testAge\n- complexity\n- codeChangeImpact\n- isPlaywright\n- criticalityLevel\n- recentFailures
    ML -> ML: calculateFailureProbability(features)
    
    alt Model trained (>50 samples)
        ML -> ML: predictWithModel(features)\nLogistic Regression
    else Fallback
        ML -> ML: weightedAverage(features)\nExpert weights
    end
    
    ML -> ML: calculateConfidence(historyCount)
    ML -> ML: explainPrediction(features)
end

ML -> ML: sortByProbability(predictions)
ML -> CLI: MLPrediction[]
deactivate ML

== Strategy Selection ==

CLI -> Strategy: selectStrategy(strategyName)
activate Strategy

alt Strategy: Quick
    Strategy -> Strategy: filterTests()\n- Select high priority\n- Limit to 60 tests\n- Target 5 min
else Strategy: Balanced
    Strategy -> Strategy: filterTests()\n- Mix critical + changed\n- Limit to 50 tests\n- Target 10 min
else Strategy: Smoke
    Strategy -> Strategy: filterTests()\n- Only critical paths\n- Limit to 15 tests\n- Target 1-2 min
else Strategy: Comprehensive
    Strategy -> Strategy: selectAllTests()\n- All tests included\n- No time limit
end

Strategy -> CLI: FilteredTestCase[]
deactivate Strategy

== Execution Planning ==

CLI -> Planner: createOptimizationPlan(filteredTests, predictions)
activate Planner

Planner -> Planner: prioritizeByRisk()\nSort by failureProbability DESC
Planner -> Planner: groupByCategory()\nauth, products, navigation, etc.
Planner -> Planner: calculateEstimatedDuration()
Planner -> Planner: generateExecutionOrder()

Planner -> DB: savePlan(optimizationPlan)
activate DB
DB -> Planner: planId
deactivate DB

Planner -> CLI: OptimizationPlan
deactivate Planner

== Test Execution ==

CLI -> Executor: executeOptimizedTests(plan)
activate Executor

loop For each test in execution order
    Executor -> Executor: setupTestEnvironment()
    Executor -> Executor: runCucumberScenario(testCase)
    
    alt Test Passes
        Executor -> Executor: recordSuccess(testCase)
    else Test Fails
        Executor -> Executor: recordFailure(testCase, error)
        Executor -> Executor: captureScreenshot()
        Executor -> Executor: saveErrorLog()
    end
    
    Executor -> DB: updateExecutionHistory(result)
    activate DB
    DB -> Executor: saved
    deactivate DB
end

Executor -> Executor: aggregateResults()
Executor -> CLI: TestResult[]
deactivate Executor

== ML Model Update ==

CLI -> ML: updateModel(testResults)
activate ML

ML -> ML: extractFeaturesFromResults()
ML -> ML: addTrainingData(features, labels)
ML -> ML: keepRecentSamples(1000)

alt trainingData.length >= 50
    ML -> ML: retrainModel()\n- Simple gradient descent\n- 100 epochs\n- Learning rate: 0.01
    ML -> ML: updateWeights()
end

ML -> ML: calculateMetrics()\n- Accuracy\n- Precision\n- Recall\n- F1 Score

ML -> DB: saveModelState()
activate DB
DB -> ML: saved
deactivate DB

ML -> CLI: modelMetrics
deactivate ML

== Report Generation ==

CLI -> Reporter: generateReport(plan, results, metrics)
activate Reporter

Reporter -> Reporter: calculateStatistics()\n- Total tests run\n- Pass/Fail ratio\n- Time saved\n- Coverage metrics

Reporter -> Reporter: createHTMLReport()
Reporter -> Reporter: createJSONReport()

Reporter -> Reporter: saveReport(test-optimizer-reports/)
Reporter -> CLI: reportPaths[]
deactivate Reporter

CLI -> GH: exitCode, reportPaths
deactivate CLI

== Artifact Upload ==

GH -> GH: uploadArtifacts(reports)
GH -> GH: postPRComment(summary)
GH -> Developer: ✅ Test optimization complete
deactivate GH

== Continuous Learning ==

note over DB, ML
Every execution improves the model:
- New test results → Training data
- Model retrains automatically
- Predictions become more accurate
- Optimization improves over time
end note

@enduml
